<quest quest_id="12" category="training_quest" tag="Silver Lining" published="False" valid="True">
	<title>Silver Lining</title>
	<description>Learn more about how $[Skill.S.s_salvaging_NameSingular] and the  $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NamePlural] work</description>
	<nodes>
		<node type="start_node" id="0" tag="">
			<conditions>
				<condition type="quest_completion" id="10" value="1" tag="A Quest Completion Condition" quest_id="13" />
			</conditions>
		</node>
		<node type="end_node" id="1" tag="">
			<actions>
				<action type="give_item_to_player" id="4" tag="An Add Item(s) to Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Telescope" quantity="1" inventory_type="Bank" />
			</actions>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="2" tag="talk to merchant" optional_tasks="True">
			<instruction>Talk to any merchant in a safe city</instruction>
			<journal_entry>Buying and selling is an art in itself - nothing should go to waste. It might surprise you, but every broken piece of weapon or armor, tattered robe or rusty armor still has value. They can be salvaged at a $[Resource.W.r_workbench_NameSingular] or a $[Resource.A.r_anvil_NameSingular] using your  $[Skill.S.s_salvaging_NameSingular] skill. Once salvaged, each item is broken down to some of its original materials which can then be sold back or gathered to craft brand new items. Items will naturally deteriorate the more they are being used and will eventually end up as $[Resource.S.r_salvagables_NameSingular]. Monsters in the safe zones might carry something worth salvaging, but it is the ocean bottoms that are really filled with $[Resource.S.r_salvagables_NameSingular]. The only catch is that you need a $[Resource.F.r_figurine_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular] to make some real profit out of $[Skill.S.s_salvaging_NameSingular]. For starters, try getting some salvage off a monster.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="interact_with_vendor" id="0" value="1" tag="An Interact With Vendor Task" vendor_id="j15_urranyr_merchant" />
				<task type="interact_with_vendor" id="1" value="1" tag="An Interact With Vendor Task" vendor_id="k13_lyran_merchant" />
				<task type="interact_with_vendor" id="2" value="1" tag="An Interact With Vendor Task" vendor_id="k14_amurran_merchant" />
