		<node type="event_simple" id="3" tag="" optional_tasks="False">
			<instruction>Gather some of the materials for a $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular]</instruction>
			<journal_entry>Now that you have the required materials, bring them to a merchant and they will take care of the rest.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="gather_items" id="18" value="1" tag="A Gather Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_Gold" quantity="5000" inventory_type="Backpack, Bank">
					<task_instruction>Gather 5,000 $[Resource.G.r_gold_NameSingular] in your bank</task_instruction>
				</task>
				<task type="gather_items" id="19" value="1" tag="A Gather Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_new Module Ship" quantity="7" inventory_type="Backpack, Bank">
					<task_instruction>Gather 15 $[Resource.M.r_module_ship_NamePlural] in your bank</task_instruction>
				</task>
				<task type="gather_items" id="20" value="1" tag="A Gather Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_Ship Cannon Item" quantity="1" inventory_type="Backpack, Bank">
					<task_instruction>Gather 1 $[Resource.S.r_ship_cannon_item_NameSingular] in your bank</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="4" tag="loot some salvage">
			<instruction>Gather some pieces of broken weapons from a gravestone.</instruction>
			<journal_entry>Now that you&apos;ve acquired something worth salvaging, you should have a go at actually breaking it down for its materials at a $[Resource.W.r_workbench_NameSingular] or a $[Resource.A.r_anvil_NameSingular]. Don&apos;t forget that you will probably get only a few materials back without much value, but the higher the amount and quality of the materials that were put into crafting the original item, the higher the payout when salvaging the useless, broken variety.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="loot_object" id="16" value="1" tag="A Loot Object Task" resource_name="r_Grounded Monsters" />
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="5" tag="r_Salvagables or r_Salvage">
			<instruction>Salvage some broken piece of armor or weapon</instruction>
			<journal_entry>While searching for monsters that drop salvageable materials seems like it&apos;s not worth it, it is quite a different story when you are out in the sea at the helm of a $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular]. There are so many salvageable materials waiting to be brought onto the ship and then broken down for profit. For you, we&apos;ve got a special, one time offer with one of our shipbuilding partners. Gather nearly half of the materials required for a $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular] and we will fill in the rest. Don&apos;t worry though, it&apos;ll be just as watertight as the rest!</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="use_skill_on" id="17" value="1" tag="A Use Skill On Object Task" resource_name="r_Salvage" skill_name="s_Salvaging" />
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_merge" id="6" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Thanks for the materials and your generous contribution. Here&apos;s your brand new $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular]. It should serve you well, at least for a while.</journal_entry>
			<actions>
				<action type="take_item_from_player" id="0" tag="A Take Item(s) from Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Gold" quantity="5000" inventory_type="Backpack" />
				<action type="take_item_from_player" id="1" tag="A Take Item(s) from Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_new Module Ship" quantity="7" inventory_type="Backpack" />
				<action type="take_item_from_player" id="2" tag="A Take Item(s) from Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Ship Cannon Item" quantity="1" inventory_type="Bank" />
			</actions>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="8" tag="">
			<journal_entry>There you go! Double-click it while pointing out towards the sea, hop in and start scraping! Watch out for pirates though!</journal_entry>
			<actions>
				<action type="give_item_to_player" id="3" tag="An Add Item(s) to Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Figurine Ship Sea Scraper" quantity="1" inventory_type="Backpack" />
			</actions>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="9" tag="" optional_tasks="False">
			<instruction>Go scraping with your new $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular]</instruction>
			<journal_entry>Well it seems like a profitable venture if everything goes right, doesn&apos;t it? Just in case, we placed a $[Resource.T.r_telescope_NameSingular] to your $[Resource.B.r_bank_NameSingular] - it&apos;ll help you see ships in the vicinity. Be very careful while you&apos;re scraping away - you will still have to empty whatever you scrape from your ship&apos;s $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_shipbox_NameSingular] and carry it before you are able to salvage it properly.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="activate_item" id="38" value="1" tag="An Activate Item Task" resource_name="r_Figurine Ship Sea Scraper" consume="False">
					<task_instruction>Deploy your $[Resource.S.r_ship_fishing_trawler_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
				<task type="harvest_resource" id="39" value="1" tag="A Harvest Resource(s) Task" resource_name="r_Salvage" quantity="48">
					<task_instruction>Harvest four dozen pieces of $[Resource.S.r_salvagables_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
